+## The capture folder
+`<id>/capture/` holds the capture's record: `ask.md`, `idea-review-NNN.md` (the reviewer's, numbered by the dispatcher) and `idea-refute-NNN.md` (yours). The gate's audit checks them (`./zn audit`, `z-nile/engine/capturecheck.luau`): an issue with a `capture/ask.md` must have all of the following, and one without a `capture/` folder is not checked (every issue before c0260). `ask.md`:
+
+````markdown
+# Ask for <id>
+
+## Verbatim ask
+```
+<the user's words, exactly>
+```
+
+## Part
+<only in a batch: the sibling ids, and this issue's part quoted>
+
+## Interview
+### Q1
+Question: <exactly as asked>
+Options: <the options offered, or "free text">
+Answer: <the user's words, exactly>
+### Q2
+...
+
+## Confirmation
+Confirmed (user, YYYY-MM-DD) after idea-review-NNN: "<the user's words>"
+````
+
+`## Part` is present only for a batch capture. `## Interview` holds `### Qn` blocks numbered from 1 without gaps, each with its `Question:`, `Options:` and `Answer:` lines, or the single line `None: <why>`. `NNN` in the Confirmation line is the highest `idea-review-NNN.md` in the folder. Every `### Fn` finding of each review has a line `- Fn: fixed|refuted|ask: …` in the same-numbered `idea-refute-NNN.md`; an `ask:` line is kept only while the Confirmation is `unattended`. A fenced block is the user's words as written: nothing inside it is a heading or a field, and an unclosed fence is an error. `./zn land` lets a later land add questions and change the Confirmation, and refuses a change to the Verbatim ask, the Part, an existing question or any landed `idea-review-NNN.md`; it also refuses the capture files of an issue another terminal has already claimed.
 
 ## Headless (under `./zn dispatch`)
 When `ZN_DISPATCH=1` is set you run headless and unattended, with the agent's own GitHub credential, and nobody answers a question. Never decide what you would ask the user (a scope change, a final review round that goes to the user, a missing credential): write the questions to `$ZN_DISPATCH_DIR/questions.md`, one `## Q<n>` heading per question with the options and what each costs, and stop. The dispatcher stops the chain there until the user answers and runs `./zn dispatch retry <id>`. `./zn land`, `status`, `spend` and every other `./zn` command that publishes tracker state are allowed: the dispatcher pushes that tracker state to `main` for you. Never `git push` to `main` and never merge a pull request: the dispatcher merges at its gates, your credential can't, and `z-nile/bin/git` and `gh` refuse. Record your spend as this skill says, but without `--tokens` for your own session: the dispatcher records the session's tokens and model. Start every review with `./zn dispatch zz-review <id> --mode <design|raft|code|stream>` (zz-rules skill, Dispatch), and give that one command a two-hour timeout (in Claude Code, the Bash tool's `timeout` of 7200000 ms): a review takes minutes, and the dispatcher keeps it alive by its heartbeat.
 
+## A capture under the dispatcher
+This is the one exception to the stop-and-ask above, for the interview and the confirmation: a capture does not stop for the user (a stop after `./zn new` would leave a stub that a retry duplicates, and `./zn dispatch retry` keeps no description for a new capture). Under the dispatcher the ask is the description you were given, and the user who started the dispatch is the only confirmation there is:
+- Step 1 as usual: the description, verbatim, in `capture/ask.md`.
+- Step 2: nobody can be asked, so the Interview is the single line `None: unattended, nobody could be asked`. Every question you would have asked is instead kept as an open point: a finding of step 6 answered `- Fn: ask: <the question and the options>`.
+- Step 6 as usual (`./zn dispatch zz-review <id> --mode idea` is allowed here, with its two-hour timeout); a finding that needs the user is answered `ask:`, and the idea is not changed to a guess.
+- Step 7 is the Confirmation line `Confirmed (unattended, YYYY-MM-DD) after idea-review-NNN: the user started this dispatch with this ask`. That is not the user's confirmation of the idea: z-design shows the user the clean idea and every `ask:` line before it designs, and replaces this line with theirs (z-design skill, The capture folder); the audit refuses a designed issue that still says `unattended`.
+- Step 8: land without asking; the dispatcher pushes the capture for you.
+
